        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          For standard local RAG pipelines, pairing <code class="text-emerald-300 font-mono text-xs">nomic-embed-text</code> with PostgreSQL pgvector offers the optimal combination: high semantic precision, an expansive 8,192-token context window that accommodates large code or document chunks, and sub-15ms embedding generation on modest GPU hardware.
        </p>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          When segmenting documents for vector indexing, adopt a chunking window of 512 to 1,024 tokens with a 10% to 15% overlap window. This guarantees that semantic context spanning across sentence or paragraph boundaries is preserved in adjacent vector embeddings, preventing retrieval fragmentation when answering nuanced technical questions.
        </p>
